"not-every-hir-is-damage"},["STRONG",{"class":"co-title"},"Not every ",["CODE",{},"$HIR"]," is damage."],["P",{},"Pickups, heals and status effects arrive on the same message type — the protocol/subtype tells you which row fired."],["P",{"class":"src"},["SPAN",{},"Source:"]," ",["A",{"href":"https://github.com/tony99nyr/open-brx/blob/main/protocol/brx-protocol.md","rel":"noopener"},"protocol/brx-protocol.md"]," §7k"]]],"\n",["SECTION",{"class":"blk blk-table","data-type":"table"},["H2",{"id":"the-other-events"},"The other events"],["DIV",{"class":"table-wrap"},["TABLE",{},"\n",["THEAD",{},"\n",["TR",{},"\n",["TH",{},"Message"],"\n",["TH",{},"Decode"],"\n",["TH",{},"Conf"],"\n"],"\n"],"\n",["TBODY",{},["TR",{},"\n",["TD",{},["CODE",{},"$HP,<hp>,<armor>,<shield>,*"]],"\n",["TD",{},"Pools after the hit; same millisecond as its ",["CODE",{},"$HIR"],". ",["CODE",{},"$HP,0,0,0"]," = death. Example run at 9/hit: armor 70→61→…→0, then HP 45→43→34→…→0. Writes (",["CODE",{},"$LIFE"],"/",["CODE",{},"$BUMP"],") do not self-emit ",["CODE",{},"$HP"],"."],"\n",["TD",{},["SPAN",{"class":"badge b-bench","title":"Verified on our bench"},["I",{"aria-hidden":"true"},"✅"],["SPAN",{},"bench"]]],"\n"],"\n",["TR",{},"\n",["TD",{},["CODE",{},"$LCD,<hp>,<armor>,<t3>,<t4>,<mag>,<reserve>,*"]],"\n",["TD",{},"Health/armor HUD echo on ",["CODE",{},"$START"],"/",["CODE",{},"$SPAWN"],"/death. Tokens 3–4: — (unknown)."],"\n",["TD",{},["SPAN",{"class":"badge b-bench","title":"Verified on our bench"},["I",{"aria-hidden":"true"},"✅"],["SPAN",{},"bench"]]],"\n"],"\n",["TR",{},"\n",["TD",{},["CODE",{},"$ALCD,<mag>,<t2>,<slot>,<reserve>,<heat>,*"]],"\n",["TD",{},"Ammo/weapon HUD (token 2: — (unknown)): one frame per round fired ",["EM",{},"and"]," per round reloaded; slot changes on alt-fire cycle (0↔1); melee (slot 4) appears as an isolated frame. Heat is a raw level that exceeds 100."],"\n",["TD",{},["SPAN",{"class":"badge b-bench","title":"Verified on our bench"},["I",{"aria-hidden":"true"},"✅"],["SPAN",{},"bench"]]],"\n"],"\n",["TR",{},"\n",["TD",{},["CODE",{},"$BUT,<id>,<state>,*"]],"\n",["TD",{},"0 trigger · 1 alt-fire · 2 reload handle · 3 select · 4 left · 5 right; 1 press / 0 release. In phone mode pre-game the trigger reports but does not fire."],"\n",["TD",{},["SPAN",{"class":"badge b-bench","title":"Verified on our bench"},["I",{"aria-hidden":"true"},"✅"],["SPAN",{},"bench"]]],"\n"],"\n",["TR",{},"\n",["TD",{},["CODE",{},"$VOLTS,<pack_mV>,<cell_mV>,<n3>,<n4>,*"]],"\n",["TD",{},"Battery every ~30 s in app mode. ",["STRONG",{},"Only reliably returned at good RSSI"]," — weak-signal guns in a fleet sweep returned none."],"\n",["TD",{},["SPAN",{"class":"badge b-bench","title":"Verified on our bench"},["I",{"aria-hidden":"true"},"✅"],["SPAN",{},"bench"]]],"\n"],"\n",["TR",{},"\n",["TD",{},["CODE",{},"$DISCONNECT,*"]],"\n",["TD",{},"The gun is hanging up (headset switched off, or the app closing)."],"\n",["TD",{},["SPAN",{"class":"badge b-bench","title":"Verified on our bench"},["I",{"aria-hidden":"true"},"✅"],["SPAN",{},"bench"]]],"\n"],"\n"]]],"\n",["P",{"class":"src"},["SPAN",{},"Source:"]," ",["A",{"href":"https://github.com/tony99nyr/open-brx/blob/main/protocol/brx-protocol.md","rel":"noopener"},"protocol/brx-protocol.md"]," §4, §7f, §7j, §7q, §7r; ",["A",{"href":"https://github.com/tony99nyr/open-brx/blob/main/docs/experiment-log.md","rel":"noopener"},"docs/experiment-log.md"]," (2026-08-24 fleet sweep); ",["A",{"href":"https://github.com/tony99nyr/open-brx/blob/main/docs/gotchas.md","rel":"noopener"},"docs/gotchas.md"]]],"\n",["SECTION",{"class":"blk blk-callout co-warn","data-type":"callout"},["ASIDE",{"class":"callout warn","role":"note","id":"the-gun-keeps-no-game-state-proven-three-ways"},["STRONG",{"class":"co-title"},"The gun keeps no game state — proven three ways."],["P",{},"(1) Three captures at respawn 5/15/30 s: byte-identical config, nothing on the wire encodes respawn or clock. (2) The complete end-of-game tail is ",["CODE",{},"$VOL → $HLED → $STOP → $CLEAR → $PLAY"]," — ",["STRONG",{},"the app never asks the gun for a score"],". (3) Reconnecting after out-of-range play yields zero frames, and bare ",["CODE",{},"$UP,*"]," gets no reply. The phone tallies ",["CODE",{},"$HIR"],"/",["CODE",{},"$HP"]," live; it is the only place the score ever existed. Anything needing respawn, a clock or scoring needs a host in range for the whole match."],["P",{"class":"src"},["SPAN",{},"Source:"]," ",["A",{"href":"https://github.com/tony99nyr/open-brx/blob/main/protocol/brx-protocol.md","rel":"noopener"},"protocol/brx-protocol.md"]," §7l, §7n"]]],"\n",["SECTION",{"class":"blk blk-diagram","data-type":"diagram"},["FIGURE",{"class":"fig fig-svg fig-pending","id":"DEV-08","style":"--ratio:16/9"},["DIV",{"class":"ph ph-svg","role":"img","aria-label":"Kill attribution sequence with three lifelines: VICTIM GUN, HOST, SHOOTER GUN. Victim → host: `$HIR,4,0,19,2,9,0,3` (×N) then `$HIR` + `$HP,0,0,0` (same ms). Host box: \"credit player 19 / team 2\". Host → shooter: `$SFLASH,*` (+0.4 s), `$PLAY,,4,6,V3A,,,,*` (+0.2 s), `$PLAY,,4,6,VB17,,,,*` (lead change only). Host → victim after respawn delay: `$SPAWN,,*`."},["SPAN",{"class":"ph-id"},"DEV-08"],["SPAN",{"class":"ph-kind"},"diagram pending"]],["FIGCAPTION",{},"Kill attribution + feedback sequence: victim gun → ",["CODE",{},"$HIR,…,<id>,<team>,…"]," + ",["CODE",{},"$HP,0,0,0"]," → host credits ",["CODE",{},"<id>"]," → host sends shooter gun ",["CODE",{},"$SFLASH,*"]," then ",["CODE",{},"$PLAY,,4,6,V3A,,,,*"]," (~0.4 s) and, on a lead change, ",["CODE",{},"$PLAY,,4,6,VB17,,,,*"],"."]],["P",{"class":"src"},["SPAN",{},"Source:"]," ",["A",{"href":"https://github.com/tony99nyr/open-brx/blob/main/protocol/brx-protocol.md","rel":"noopener"},"protocol/brx-protocol.md"]," §7o, §7q"]],"\n",["SECTION",{"class":"blk blk-steps","data-type":"steps"},["H2",{"id":"per-player-attribution-and-native-kill-feedback-over-ble-the"},"Per-player attribution and native kill feedback over BLE — the recipe"],["DIV",{"class":"steps"},["OL",{},"\n",["LI",{},"At arm time give every gun a distinct ",["CODE",{},"$PSET"]," token 1 (0–63) and a ",["CODE",{},"$TID"],"."],"\n",["LI",{},"On the victim, store ",["CODE",{},"<shooterId, shooterTeam>"]," from each ",["CODE",{},"$HIR"],"; when ",["CODE",{},"$HP,0,0,0"]," arrives, the stored shooter gets the kill."],"\n",["LI",{},"Send the ",["STRONG",{},"shooter's"]," gun ",["CODE",{},"$SFLASH,*"]," (green-sight kill confirm) and ",["CODE",{},"$PLAY,,4,6,V3A,,,,*"]," (\"kill\" on the announcer slot). The official app does exactly this, three kills → three pairs."],"\n",["LI",{},"Score lines (",["CODE",{},"VB17"]," \"takes the lead\") go to every gun's announcer slot from its own host. Nothing propagates gun-to-gun; there is no nRF score channel to discover."],"\n",["LI",{},"Game end: ",["CODE",{},"$PLAY,VSF,4,6,JAY,,,,*"]," on the winner's guns (victory sting + \"victory\")."],"\n"],"\n"],["P",{"class":"src"},["SPAN",{},"Source:"]," ",["A",{"href":"https://github.com/tony99nyr/open-brx/blob/main/protocol/brx-protocol.md","rel":"noopener"},"protocol/brx-protocol.md"]," §4 (kill attribution pattern), §7o, §7p, §7q, §7r"]],"\n",["SECTION",{"class":"blk blk-faq","data-type":"faq"},["DIV",{"class":"faq"},["DETAILS",{},["SUMMARY",{},"Why did earlier captures show shooter id 0,0?"],["DIV",{},["P",{},"Every gun sat on the default id. The field was always there; ",["CODE",{},"$PSET"]," token 1 is what makes it vary."],"\n"]],["DETAILS",{},["SUMMARY",{},"Why is ",["CODE",{},"$SFLASH"]," in the victim's capture \"never near a hit\"?"],["DIV",{},["P",{},"Because a kill you ",["EM",{},"score"]," is invisible in your own ",["CODE",{},"$HIR"],"/",["CODE",{},"$HP"]," stream — correlate it with ",["CODE",{},"$BUT"]," trigger bursts."],"\n"]],["DETAILS",{},["SUMMARY",{},"Can a dead gun fire?"],["DIV",{},["P",{},"No: ",["CODE",{},"$BUT,0,1/0"]," with no ",["CODE",{},"$ALCD"]," decrement."],"\n"]]],["P",{"class":"src"},["SPAN",{},"Source:"]," ",["A",{"href":"https://github.com/tony99nyr/open-brx/blob/main/protocol/brx-protocol.md","rel":"noopener"},"protocol/brx-protocol.md"]," §7q · ",["A",{"href":"https://github.com/tony99nyr/open-brx/blob/main/protocol/brx-protocol.md","rel":"noopener"},"protocol/brx-protocol.md"]," §7o · ",["A",{"href":"https://github.com/tony99nyr/open-brx/blob/main/protocol/brx-protocol.md","rel":"noopener"},"protocol/brx-protocol.md"]," §7q"]],"\n\n"],"\n  "],"\n  ",["ASIDE",{"class":"toc","aria-label":"On this page"},["DIV",{"class":"toc-in"},["P",{"class":"toc-h"},"On this page"],["OL",{},["LI",{},["A",{"href":"#hir"},"$HIR,<sensor>,<irProto>,<shooterId>,<shooterTeam>,<magnitude>,<crit>,<subtype>,"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"#not-every-hir-is-damage"},"Not every $HIR is damage."]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"#the-other-events"},"The other events"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"#the-gun-keeps-no-game-state-proven-three-ways"},"The gun keeps no game state — proven three ways."]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"#per-player-attribution-and-native-kill-feedback-over-ble-the"},"Per-player attribution and native kill feedback over BLE — the recipe"]]]]],"\n"],"\n",["FOOTER",{"class":"foot"},"\n  ",["P",{},"Protocol discovered by ",["A",{"href":"https://github.com/LaserTagMods","rel":"noopener"},"LaserTagMods"]," (JEDGE / JBOX) · Hardware by Battle Company · Fixes by the owner community."],"\n  ",["P",{},"Open BRX is an independent open-source project and is not affiliated with or endorsed by Battle Company. MIT licence. ",["A",{"href":"/credits/"},"Credits & sourcing"]," · ",["A",{"href":"/changelog/"},"Changelog"]," · ",["A",{"href":"/llms.txt"},"llms.txt"]," · ",["A",{"href":"https://github.com/tony99nyr/open-brx","rel":"noopener"},"GitHub"]],"\n"],"\n",["DIV",{"class":"search-modal","data-search-modal":"","hidden":""},["DIV",{"class":"search-box","role":"dialog","aria-label":"Search"},["INPUT",{"__playwright_value_":"","type":"search","data-search-input":"","placeholder":"Search pages, headings, weapons, sound 