{"type":"after","callId":"call@389","endTime":52690.133,"result":{"value":{"s":"\n    Home/Manual/Developer reference/Events — what the gun tells you\n    \n\nEvents — what the gun tells you\nHits, health, HUD echoes, buttons and telemetry — and the proof that the gun keeps no game state\n✅benchLast verified 2026-08-27View as Markdown\nWhat the badges mean✅bench Verified on our bench📖official Official Battle Company docs🔍app Decoded from the Callsign app👥community Community-reported🧪software Built + software-tested📐spec Specified only🚧under construction Under constructionNothing unconfirmed is published — see Credits & sourcing.\n\n(render as labelled token boxes)\n\n\ntok\nField\nValues\nNotes\nConf\n\n\n\n1\nsensor that caught the IR\n0 headset front dome · 1 headset back dome · 4 gun body\nIsolated with every other sensor covered. Trust for directional logic only at field distance — point-blank floods every receiver and the first to decode reports.\n✅bench\n\n\n2\nshooter's IR protocol\n0 standard · 10 rocket · 13 melee …\n= the shooter's  t3 / IR word B field.\n✅bench\n\n\n3\nshooter player id\n0–63\n= the shooter's  token 1. 32/32 hits both directions on two guns with distinct ids.\n✅bench\n\n\n4\nshooter team\n0–3\n= the shooter's effective .\n✅bench\n\n\n5\nraw magnitude\ne.g. 9, 45, 80, 115\nThe IR word's D field (= shooter's t5). Not the applied damage where a multiplier row or crit is in play — derive damage from the  delta. On a killing blow it can report the victim's remaining pool instead (overkill clamp).\n✅bench\n\n\n6\ncrit flag\n0/1\nEchoes the IR word's C bit. 0 on every stock weapon.\n✅bench\n\n\n7\nsubtype\n0–3\nEchoes the IR word's U field (sniper = 1).\n✅bench\n\n\nSource: protocol/brx-protocol.md §4, §7k, §7q, §7r, §7r addendum, tok1 sensor-map section; protocol/brx-ir-protocol.md\nNot every  is damage.Pickups, heals and status effects arrive on the same message type — the protocol/subtype tells you which row fired.Source: protocol/brx-protocol.md §7k\nThe other events\n\n\nMessage\nDecode\nConf\n\n\n\n\nPools after the hit; same millisecond as its .  = death. Example run at 9/hit: armor 70→61→…→0, then HP 45→43→34→…→0. Writes (/) do not self-emit .\n✅bench\n\n\n\nHealth/armor HUD echo on //death. Tokens 3–4: — (unknown).\n✅bench\n\n\n\nAmmo/weapon HUD (token 2: — (unknown)): one frame per round fired and per round reloaded; slot changes on alt-fire cycle (0↔1); melee (slot 4) appears as an isolated frame. Heat is a raw level that exceeds 100.\n✅bench\n\n\n\n0 trigger · 1 alt-fire · 2 reload handle · 3 select · 4 left · 5 right; 1 press / 0 release. In phone mode pre-game the trigger reports but does not fire.\n✅bench\n\n\n\nBattery every ~30 s in app mode. Only reliably returned at good RSSI — weak-signal guns in a fleet sweep returned none.\n✅bench\n\n\n\nThe gun is hanging up (headset switched off, or the app closing).\n✅bench\n\n\nSource: protocol/brx-protocol.md §4, §7f, §7j, §7q, §7r; docs/experiment-log.md (2026-08-24 fleet sweep); docs/gotchas.md\nThe gun keeps no game state — proven three ways.(1) Three captures at respawn 5/15/30 s: byte-identical config, nothing on the wire encodes respawn or clock. (2) The complete end-of-game tail is  — the app never asks the gun for a score. (3) Reconnecting after out-of-range play yields zero frames, and bare  gets no reply. The phone tallies / live; it is the only place the score ever existed. Anything needing respawn, a clock or scoring needs a host in range for the whole match.Source: protocol/brx-protocol.md §7l, §7n\nDEV-08diagram pendingKill attribution + feedback sequence: victim gun →  +  → host credits  → host sends shooter gun  then  (~0.4 s) and, on a lead change, .Source: protocol/brx-protocol.md §7o, §7q\nPer-player attribution and native kill feedback over BLE — the recipe\nAt arm time give every gun a distinct  token 1 (0–63) and a .\nOn the victim, store  from each ; when  arrives, the stored shooter gets the kill.\nSend the shooter's gun  (green-sight kill confirm) and  (\"kill\" on the announcer slot). The official app does exactly this, three kills → three pairs.\nScore lines ( \"takes the lead\") go to every gun's announcer slot from its own host. Nothing propagates gun-to-gun; there is no nRF score channel to discover.\nGame end:  on the winner's guns (victory sting + \"victory\").\n\nSource: protocol/brx-protocol.md §4 (kill attribution pattern), §7o, §7p, §7q, §7r\nWhy did earlier captures show shooter id 0,0?Every gun sat on the default id. The field was always there;  token 1 is what makes it vary.\nWhy is  in the victim's capture \"never near a hit\"?Because a kill you score is invisible in your own / stream — correlate it with  trigger bursts.\nCan a dead gun fire?No:  with no  decrement.\nSource: protocol/brx-protocol.md §7q · protocol/brx-protocol.md §7o · protocol/brx-protocol.md §7q\n\n\n  "}},"afterSnapshot":"after@call@389"}
